# The quickscan archetype with probes 10 cells apart. They point inside the warrior, so no skip is
# fused: ptr is cell 86, the bomb 87. Probe 1 compares cell 10 (code: a JMP) with cell 110
# (empty): they differ, SNE skips its JMP (1), JMP to the first stub (2), which points ptr at cell 10
# (3: 10 - 86) and jumps to found (4); found bombs cell 10 (5), moves ptr by gap (6) and bombs cell
# 110 (7).
golden: bbctests/examples/quickscan_hit.bbc
hill: 94nop
cell 3 86 DAT.F #0, #-76
cell 5 10 DAT.F #0, #0
cell 7 110 DAT.F #0, #0
